      "writtenOn": "2022-02-21T01:16:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Great to see that you\u0027ve removed the fixed sleep. In order to avoid excessive CPU load, would put a sleep in this loop. If you don\u0027t know how long this takes, maybe something like SystemClock.sleep(5) or (10)?\n\nSystemClock#sleep is useful because unlike Thread.sleep it handles InterruptedException for you. That not only removes the need for a try/catch clause, but also makes the test more correct because dealing with InterruptedException is a bit tricky.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "faed3af6d5f3bd8fcc996a90f68ce8b34065a088",
